# https://manpages.debian.org/experimental/sway/sway-output.5.en.html
# https://sr.ht/~emersion/kanshi/
#
# NOTE on scale: kanshi drives Hyprland via the wlr-output-management protocol,
# which sends the scale verbatim and STRICTLY validates it. eDP-1 is 2256x1504;
# a scale of 1.333 yields a non-integer logical size (1692.42 x 1128.28), so
# Hyprland rejects the whole configuration and the panel never enables (kanshi
# still logs "applied" because the request was sent). Use 1.333333 (exactly 4/3)
# -> 1692 x 1128, which Hyprland accepts. (hyprctl/hl.monitor auto-rounds and so
# masks this; the protocol path does not.)
#
# NOTE on mode: these Dell U2518D units report NO preferred mode over EDID
# (Hyprland shows preferredMode: None). Without an explicit `mode`, kanshi/
# Hyprland fall back to 1280x720 on every dock, giving wrong resolution + DPI.
# Pin the native mode 2560x1440@59.95Hz explicitly so docking is deterministic.

profile laptop-only {
  output eDP-1 enable scale 1.333333
}

profile docked-home {
  output eDP-1 disable
  output "Dell Inc. DELL U2518D 3C4YP898AHPL" enable mode 2560x1440@59.95Hz transform 90 position 0,0
  output "Dell Inc. DELL U2518D 3C4YP8A4AGBL" enable mode 2560x1440@59.95Hz position 1440,560
}
